MAGNITUDE TREATMENT ISSUE

---makeFresFiles.pl-------------------------------------OK

- magnitudes are determined from hypothetical absolute magnitudes (Carrol and Ostlie data) and added to distance modulus, calculated from physical distance (pc) given in run.sh
- assumes distance is not calculated from appparent magnitudes, but rather from de-reddened ones...i.e. accurate
- makes Fresnel files using bandpass wavelengths, hypothetical apparent visual magnitude (dereddened), spectral type and distance (AU) to KB or OC


---makeStarDB.pl----------------------------------------OK

- parses original catalogue of apparent V and apparent B-V values
- uses distance modulus and reddening to determine absolute V
- dereddens B-V
- compares absolute V and dereddened B-V w/ Carrol and Ostlie data to determine stellar type and Teff
- uses apparent V and Teff to determine flux w/ fluxCalc
- makes star database with following info: Stellar Type, Apparent V, Dereddened B-V, Teff, Absolute V, Radius of star (Radians), Flux in photons/sec/m^2, Star Code, RA and Dec


---runKomplete.pl---------------------------------------OK

- iterates through each main sequence spectral type
- pulls out data from Carrol and Ostlie source
- constructs apparent visual magnitude by adding reddening and distance modulus to absolute magnitude
- uses this apparent visual magnitude and Teff to calculate theoretical flux value for each spectral type at said distance using fluxCalc
- uses flux value to calculate statistical parameters of PSF


---fitRminBmax.pl---------------------------------------OK

- magnitudes not used

---getRates.pl------------------------------------------OK

- at end of script, uses distance to determine distmod
- addes distmod and Av to the absolute magnitude of the limiting magnitude for a particular aperture size, which is then printed out